{
  "recommendation": "Based on the information available, the strongest fit for a $5,000 deposit appears to be a Gold Account savings account paired with a Gold Rewards Card.",
  "why": [
    "The Gold Account has a 5.5% base APY.",
    "The Gold Rewards Card reduces the Gold Account minimum balance requirement from $10,000 to $5,000, making it accessible with your current savings.",
    "The Gold Rewards Card adds a 0.025% APY relationship bonus, for an expected effective APY of approximately 5.525%.",
    "Your existing Light Blue checking account does not appear in the documented qualifying checking-savings pairings, so it would not provide a linked-account APY boost."
  ],
  "estimated_one_year_interest": {
    "deposit": 5000,
    "approximate_effective_apy": "5.525%",
    "approximate_gross_interest": "$276.25",
    "fees": "The Gold Rewards Card annual fee was not available in the information I found, so I cannot accurately calculate net earnings yet."
  },
  "important_credit_card_rule": "Use the credit card only if you can pay the statement balance in full. Carrying a balance can outweigh the savings interest because credit-card purchase APRs are much higher than savings APYs.",
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "option": "EcoCard plus Gold Account",
      "assessment": "The EcoCard provides a 0.6% APY bonus on a Gold Account, but it does not reduce the Gold Account's $10,000 minimum balance requirement. With only $5,000, this combination may not meet the account requirement."
    },
    {
      "option": "Light Blue checking plus Platinum Account",
      "assessment": "The documented 0.65% boost applies to Light Green checking, not Light Blue checking. Therefore, I cannot assume your Light Blue account would qualify."
    }
  ],
  "next_step": "To calculate the true interest-minus-fees result, I need the Gold Rewards Card annual fee and any required Gold Account maintenance fee details. I also recommend confirming whether you expect to keep the full $5,000 in savings for the entire year and whether you will pay the card in full each month."
}
